From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bachaalany <elias.bachaalany@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Decompiler: RawLoadImage robust stream reads

RawLoadImage opened the program image in TEXT mode and never checked stream
state, so one short read silently poisoned every later read of the image.

On Windows a text-mode stream treats 0x1A (Ctrl-Z) as end-of-file and collapses
CRLF. Program images are full of 0x1A bytes, so a read that loadFill had already
clamped to lie fully within the file still came up short. A short read sets
failbit (not merely eofbit); once failbit is set, every subsequent seekg/read
fails its sentry and becomes a no-op. loadFill advanced offset/size by the
REQUESTED count rather than the delivered one, so the loop still terminated and
the function returned successfully -- leaving the caller's buffer untouched.
Callers that zero-initialise their buffer therefore received zeros, silently and
permanently, for every later read.

Measured end to end in an offline decompilation of a 198-function PE: reads
returned real bytes until one function tripped the short read, then every later
read returned zeros, 132 of 198 functions decompiled to nothing, and re-opening
the program restored everything.

Three fixes: open the image binary; clear() sticky state before each seek; and
advance by gcount() so a genuine short read reports DataUnavailError instead of
being mistaken for success.
---
 .../Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/loadimage.cc | 20 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/loadimage.cc b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/loadimage.cc
index 558229946c..dafe575b6a 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/loadimage.cc
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/loadimage.cc
@@ -57,7 +57,10 @@ void RawLoadImage::open(void)
 
 {
   if (thefile != (ifstream *)0) throw LowlevelError("loadimage is already open");
-  thefile = new ifstream(filename.c_str());
+  // Must be binary: in text mode a 0x1A (Ctrl-Z) byte is treated as end-of-file
+  // on Windows and CRLF pairs are collapsed, so reads of a program image come up
+  // short even when fully in range.
+  thefile = new ifstream(filename.c_str(),ios::binary);
   if (!(*thefile)) {
     string errmsg = "Unable to open raw image file: "+filename;
     delete thefile;
@@ -98,11 +101,20 @@ void RawLoadImage::loadFill(uint1 *ptr,int4 size,const Address &addr)
     readsize = size;
     if (curaddr + readsize > filesize) // Adjust to biggest possible read
       readsize = filesize - curaddr;
+    // A short read sets failbit (not just eofbit), and once failbit is set every
+    // later seekg/read fails its sentry and becomes a silent no-op. Clearing here
+    // keeps one bad read from permanently poisoning the image for all later reads.
+    thefile->clear();
     thefile->seekg(curaddr);
     thefile->read((char *)(ptr+offset),readsize);
-    offset += readsize;
-    size -= readsize;
-    curaddr += readsize;
+    // Advance by what actually arrived, not by what was requested. Assuming
+    // readsize let a no-op read still satisfy the loop, so loadFill returned
+    // successfully while leaving the caller's buffer untouched.
+    uintb actual = (uintb)thefile->gcount();
+    if (actual == 0) break;	// No progress; report it below rather than spin
+    offset += actual;
+    size -= (int4)actual;
+    curaddr += actual;
   }
   if (size > 0) {
     ostringstream errmsg;
